  "id": "DrugBank_DB06766 - MONDO_grouped_2309_2308",
  "verbalization": "Alcaftadine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Papillary Conjunctivitis through a chain of indications that link it to Atopic Conjunctivitis, which in turn is associated with Levocabastine and Ketotifen. This suggests a potential pathway where Alcaftadine may exert some therapeutic or pathophysiological effect that is indirectly linked to the development of Papillary Conjunctivitis. The shared indication of Atopic Conjunctivitis across multiple pathways implies a possible overlap in mechanisms, such as allergic inflammation or immune response modulation. The presence of multiple overlapping indications supports the idea that Alcaftadine may influence pathways involved in conjunctival inflammation, potentially contributing to the development of Papillary Conjunctivitis. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving allergic or inflammatory processes, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear.",
